  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The table below lists the refractive indices for four different transparent substances.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Substance</th><th>Refractive Index (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n\"></span>)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Diamond</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.42\"></span></td></tr><tr><td>Flint glass</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.66\"></span></td></tr><tr><td>Water</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.33\"></span></td></tr><tr><td>Ice</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.31\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Which combination of materials and direction of light travel would result in the smallest critical angle for total internal reflection?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">From flint glass to water</li><li data-label=\"B\">From diamond to ice</li><li data-label=\"C\">From water to ice</li><li data-label=\"D\">From diamond to flint glass</li></ol>"
  },
